Z||000010||terryk||12-18-1999||01:49 AM||||loafer87gt:<P>Are you in an area the requires emissions testing? If not, I'll bet that engine could be run on an Buick ECM. 92-&gt;95-ish. DIS/MASS/SFI. You might be best off with an automatic though. I'm tuning a guys 95 3800 SC chip for use in a sand rail and the flywheel was a big issue.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||loafer87gt||12-18-1999||01:22 PM||||Emissions testing? Whats that? No, seriously I live on an acreage up here in Canada and they don't really care about emissions. As far as the different DOHC engines go, I did some research and found this out. The Shortstar is based on the Aurora 4.0 V8, which was based on the Northstar. The 3.0 DOHC in the Caterra is an Opel design, and has a 54 degree cast block instead of the lighter aluminum block of the 3.5 DOHC. Boy, if I won the lottery I would be doing one of these conversions pronto.||||reg||1
Z||000012||jhogans||12-18-1999||06:27 PM||||Raydar,<P>Ed Parks doesn't have the Northstar any longer.  I was at his shop a couple of months ago.  He had sold it for the owner's widow.||||reg||1
Z||000013||fiero56||12-18-1999||06:34 PM||||Emmisions testing is where they send a probe up your pipe, to determine your "output" <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">. It measure hydrocarbons(HC) and other contaminants produced by comnustion that are hazardous to the environment.||||reg||10
